[metadata]
Name:Rules pilot 348 - The Clone copies the mana cost
Goal:Win
Turns:1
Difficulty:Hard
Description:It is your second main phase. You control Gray Merchant of Asphodel and have Clone in hand, with four blue mana floating. The opponent is at 4 life and controls a tapped Silent Arbiter. Reduce the opponent to 0 life this turn.
Rule:authored-copy-mana-cost-devotion | A copy takes the copied object's mana cost (CR 707.2), and devotion counts the mana symbols in the mana costs of permanents you control (CR 700.5): Clone entering as Gray Merchant has {3}{B}{B}, so its own enters trigger counts devotion 4 (both Merchants) and drains 4; Clone copying the Arbiter does nothing, and the first Merchant alone counted only 2
